c expect: false
c Variable 3 is free (not in the prefix), so it is an OUTERMOST existential:
c it is chosen before x1 and cannot follow it. x1 in {0,1} needs x3 = 0,
c x1 in {2,3} needs x3 = 1 -> false. (With "e 3 0" after "a 1 0" it is true.)
c Variable 2 has domain 1, so "2:0" is always true (tautological clause).
p dcnf 3 3
d 1 2 0
d 4 1 3 0
a 1 0
-1:0,1 3:0 0
-1:2,3 3:1 0
2:0 0
